    "reply": {
      "changeSets": {
        "1": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 42,
                "quote": "Holds.queueFor book library"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 25,
                "quote": "Catalog.findBranch (BranchId branch) library"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The change adds no new domain rule. Branch lookup, hold queue order and copies-at-branch all come from Tier 2 (`Catalog.findBranch`, `Holds.queueFor`, `Catalog.copiesAt`). The Tier 3 code only projects them to CSV rows: sorting, a 1-based position, and the `on loan until` / `on shelf` label. The CLI only calls `Reports.*` and renders views. The loan-or-shelf label is a presentation projection, and I saw no existing Tier 2 definition it would contradict.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 37,
                "quote": "ports.Files.WriteLines path (\"copy,book,title,status\" :: rows)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All three new exports write through the existing `Files` port (`ports.Files.WriteLines`) and read state through `ports.Store.Load()`. There is no clock, I/O or console use below Tier 4, and the CLI does not re-enter Tier 2. The surrounding `exportOverdue` still calls `File.WriteAllLines` directly, but that line was already there and the change did not touch it.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 62,
                "quote": "Views.members (ports.Store.Load())"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The new code reuses the existing `Views.members`, `Views.date`, `Views.titleOf` and `Holds.queueFor` instead of copying their logic. No lending number, date offset or rule is restated. The CSV header strings appear once each.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 192,
                "quote": "Catalog.addCopy { Id = CopyId copyId; Book = BookId bookId; Branch = branch } library"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 35,
                "quote": "match Holds.queueFor copy.Book library with"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "Whether a copy may be added (duplicate or unknown copy or book, per DEC-011) is decided by Tier 2 `Catalog.addCopy`. `importCopies` only splits CSV lines, numbers them, and folds the results, which stops at the first error. That is boundary translation and orchestration, not a second rule. The hold count shown in the inventory comes from Tier 2 `Holds.queueFor`. The CLI only dispatches and renders.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 180,
                "quote": "match ports.Files.ReadLines path with"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The file is read through the existing `Files` port. The result goes through the existing `commit ports` path, which carries out the Store write. Nothing below Tier 4 performs I/O, and the CLI does not call Tier 2. The `backup` branch of the CLI uses `JsonFileStore` directly, but that line was already there and the change only shows it as context.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 35,
                "quote": "| queue -> $\"on shelf ({queue.Length} holds waiting)\""
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The hold count is derived from the single `Holds.queueFor` definition rather than a restated predicate. Copy validation is delegated to `Catalog.addCopy`. The line-numbered error reuses `Views.describeError`. The new `import-copies` help line appears once in `usage` and once in the README. No fact is defined twice.",
            "score": 2
          }
        }
      },
